From 532449c242540e541dd47b6225c6141547fa3b61 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: t <tristan75015@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 06:46:53 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Non linear solvers, residual: work vectors kept between the
 calls

On a GPU, a vector of MFEM created in a function is allocated on the device
at its first use and freed at the end of the function. When MFEM has no
pool of memory (MFEM built without Umpire), each of these allocations is a
call to the allocator of the GPU, whose time may be much larger than the
one of the computations of an iteration: on 256 MI300A, each allocation of
a vector of unknowns took a fixed time of 0.2 s on one or two processes,
the others waiting for them.

The vectors of a resolution are now kept by the non linear solvers
(`NonLinearSolverBase::getWorkVector`: residual, correction, estimates,
residual of the linear solve), as the residual and the correction of
`mfem::NewtonSolver`, for the Newton and fixed point solvers and for the
residual of the KINSOL and SNES solvers. The ones of the evaluations of the
residual are kept by the problem (`ResidualWorkVectors`): the inner forces
computed by kernels on the true degrees of freedom, which the
`AddMultTranspose` of `mfem::Operator` allocated at each call for the
prolongation of a conforming parallel space, and the residual of the
default prediction computed by the prediction by linear extrapolation.

The operations are the same, on the same values: the results are unchanged,
bit for bit.
